armacraft graphics patch 0002 -- UNAPPLIED. Ride trails are never lowered (CAMERA_VISIBILITY_LOWER_WALL is rim-only).

User decision (2026-10-02): keep the ride trail full height, like Armagetron. In Armagetron 0.4 the camera-visibility
lowering is implemented only for rim walls (gWallRim::OnBlocksCamera, gWall.cpp 504-526); player walls inherit the
no-op (eWall.cpp 319), so a cycle's own wall is never lowered. ArmaTrailVisual applied the rim rule to ride trails
whenever the ride camera was active and CAMERA_VISIBILITY_LOWER_WALL was on (the default 1, and the fallback for this
user's profile), so the corner wall behind the bike dropped to ~half height right after every turn.

Change:
- ArmaTrailVisual: no lowering at all. Removed the per-segment lowering state (`lowered` map, loweredHeight,
  segmentKey) and the sight-line test; every segment is drawn at the ribbon height. The rule is stated in
  `lowersTrailWalls(rideCameraActive, cameraVisibilityLowerWall)`, which returns false for every input.
- Arena mode is untouched: rim walls are still lowered by ArenaRenderer / ArenaMesher (separate code).
- ArmaTrailVisualTest.rideTrailsAreNeverLowered: the rule holds for camera active + LOWER_WALL 1, and the other
  combinations.
The `blocksPerUnit` constructor argument stays, so ArmaRideVisuals and the tests compile unchanged.

Checked (2026-10-02, scratch copy of client/ as of 16:30 BST, built against host/):
- git apply --check against client/: clean.
- ./gradlew jar test: BUILD SUCCESSFUL, 67 tests, 0 failures (1 skipped, pre-existing).
- In game (play-shaders-tex, Complementary + Euphoria, 1468x900) with the patched jar and
  ride.arma_settings.CAMERA_VISIBILITY_LOWER_WALL forced to "1": screenshots taken 0.35 s after turns, from the
  chase camera behind the bike, show the corner wall at full height:
  .work/play-shaders-tex/run-client/screenshots/bench_user1_trail_behind_{day_a,day_b,sunset,night}.png
Apply from the repo root:  git apply docs/graphics-patches/0002-client-ride-trails-never-lowered.patch

